  {
   "id": "ex1",
   "type": "example",
   "problem": {
    "en": "p: 3 is a factor of 12. q: 3 is a factor of 14. Find the truth values of p ∧ q, p ∨ q and ~(p ∧ q), and write ~(p ∧ q) in words."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "p is true (12 = 3 × 4); q is false."
    },
    {
     "en": "p ∧ q is false; p ∨ q is true; ~(p ∧ q) is true."
    },
    {
     "en": "By De Morgan, ~(p ∧ q): 3 is not a factor of 12 or 3 is not a factor of 14."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "F, T, T"
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us solve this together. p: 3 is a factor of 12. q: 3 is a factor of 14. Find the truth values of p ∧ q, p ∨ q and ~(p ∧ q), and write ~(p ∧ q) in words."
   }
